I think the patient is not complaining about bending his arm, but about
having it bent for him. I like auto-pick-up, and used it most of the
time in 3.0, but it is unplayable in 3.1. 
The good wizard obviously had this mode enabled. An unfortunate side
effect of the (excellent) new carrying system.

On this subject.....
Has anyone noticed the slight bug which occurs when your knapsack is
full. If it is full, and you have, for example, the inventory space 

a - uncursed scroll of enchant weapon.

If you then find another uncursed scroll of enchant weapon, you 
can't pick it up, because it says you knapsack is full, even though it
goes in the same inventory slot. But if you drop another item, you can
then pick it up, it gets put in slot 'a' with your other scroll, and
you can then pick up again the item that you dropped.
When your knapsack is full, it should check whether the item you are
trying to pick up already has a space in the inventory.
Like I said, however, a SLIGHT bug. I'm not trying to be picky.

